        "policy_violations": [],
        "final_response": "I implemented the six endpoints, but I couldn't build or run any of it. This environment has no `mvn` and no `java`/`javac`. The code has therefore never been compiled, and none of the contract behaviours have been tested.\n\n**Files created** in `financial-monolith/src/main/java/com/juanesteban/tcc/finance/`:\n- `User.java`, `Holding.java`, `Trade.java`: JPA entities.\n- `Repositories.java`: Spring Data repositories.\n- `ApiException.java`: exception carrying an HTTP status.\n- `FinanceService.java`: fixed quotes and the business rules.\n- `FinanceController.java`: the REST endpoints and the error handler.\n\nI changed no existing file: `pom.xml`, `application.yml`, `docker-compose.yml` and the main application class are untouched.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Users:** a new user gets 10000.00. A duplicate username returns 400.\n- **Trades:** a BUY or SELL returns 201. Shares ≤ 0, an unknown symbol, insufficient cash or an insufficient position return 400. An unknown user returns 404.\n- **Order of checks:** I validate shares and symbol before looking up the user. A request with both a bad symbol and an unknown user therefore returns 400, not 404. The contract doesn't say which should win.\n- **Atomicity:** a trade runs in one transaction and locks the user row, so a rejected trade changes nothing.\n- **Portfolio:** it returns both `cash` and `cashBalance`, plus `holdings` and `totalValue`. Each holding has `symbol`, `shares`, `price` and `marketValue`.\n- **History:** the trades endpoint returns an array with `type` set to `BUY` or `SELL`.\n\n**Commands run:** file inspection, and one `mvn` attempt that failed with `mvn: command not found`.\n\n**Next step:** run `mvn -DskipTests package` somewhere Maven and Java 21 are available to catch compile errors.",
